1
00:00:05,320 --> 00:00:07,400
这是从未有过的古怪想法
There's never been a stranger idea

2
00:00:07,510 --> 00:00:09,690
整个科学史上
in the entire history of science.

3
00:00:10,820 --> 00:00:12,880
下至最小的层面
Down at the smallest scale.

4
00:00:12,990 --> 00:00:14,670
比我们的细胞还小
Smaller than our cells.

5
00:00:15,550 --> 00:00:21,710
比原子还小 可以突然之间变大…
Smaller than atoms,could the world suddenly get bigger...

6
00:00:21,820 --> 00:00:26,290
以全新的完全出乎意料的方式扩大么？
Branching out in new and totally unexpected ways?

7
00:00:26,410 --> 00:00:30,720
了解现实的终极性质的需求
A quest to understand the ultimate nature of reality

8
00:00:30,840 --> 00:00:33,660
吸引了世上最伟大的头脑
has gripped the greatest living minds

9
00:00:33,770 --> 00:00:38,730
正迫使我们去考虑一个令人震颤的可能性…
and is forcing us to consider a truly shocking possibility...

10
00:00:38,840 --> 00:00:41,110
是否不止三维么？
Are there more than three dimensions?

11
00:00:46,860 --> 00:00:51,230
空间 时间 生命本身
Space,time,life itself.

12
00:00:53,870 --> 00:00:58,000
宇宙的秘密，尽在穿越虫洞
The secrets of the cosmos lie through the wormhole.

13
00:01:01,400 --> 00:01:05,400
是否不止三维？
Are There More Than Three Dimensions?

14
00:01:09,530 --> 00:01:16,190
上下 前后 左右
Up,down,backward,forward,side to side.

15
00:01:16,300 --> 00:01:18,960
若你想去地球上任何地方
If you want to get anywhere on Earth,

16
00:01:19,070 --> 00:01:22,560
这三个维度是你前往的唯一途径
these three dimensions are the only ways you can go.

17
00:01:22,680 --> 00:01:26,710
它们描述了我们现实中的任何地方
They describe any place in our reality.

18
00:01:27,050 --> 00:01:28,680
它们行么？
Or do they?

19
00:01:28,800 --> 00:01:30,090
许多科学家现在相信
Many scientists now believe

20
00:01:30,200 --> 00:01:32,760
我们的世界并不是三维的
our world is not three-dimensional.

21
00:01:32,870 --> 00:01:38,160
不管怎样… 还有其它移动的途径
That somehow... there are other ways to move.

22
00:01:38,280 --> 00:01:40,100
探索那些隐藏的维度
Discovering those hidden dimensions

23
00:01:40,210 --> 00:01:43,510
是物理学最有价值的东西
is the biggest prize in physics

24
00:01:43,620 --> 00:01:47,060
将会永远改变我们观察宇宙的方式
and would forever change the way we see the Universe.

25
00:01:51,060 --> 00:01:53,290
我还是密西西比三角洲的一个小孩的时候
When I was a boy down in the Mississippi Delta,

26
00:01:53,400 --> 00:01:57,790
长长夏日 虫子云集
bugs swarmed all summer long.

27
00:01:57,910 --> 00:02:01,100
其中有些甚至可以水上漂
Some of them could even walk on water.

28
00:02:01,210 --> 00:02:03,730
但其下面有些动物
But down below there were creatures

29
00:02:03,850 --> 00:02:08,320
偶尔会飞身跃起 抓住毫不知情的虫子
who would occasionally dart up and grab an unsuspecting bug.

30
00:02:10,620 --> 00:02:15,880
水虫永远都看不到它的到来
The water bugs never seemed to see it coming.

31
00:02:15,990 --> 00:02:17,550
为什么呢？
Why not?

32
00:02:17,660 --> 00:02:19,950
是不是因为对于它们来说 池塘没有深度
Was it because,to them,the pool had no depth,

33
00:02:20,070 --> 00:02:22,770
没有第三维度呢？
no third dimension?

34
00:02:26,600 --> 00:02:29,090
我们会像水虫那样
Could we be like water bugs,

35
00:02:29,210 --> 00:02:34,070
无法看到现实的全貌呢？
unable to see the full extent of reality?

36
00:02:34,180 --> 00:02:38,240
苏珊.巴里对人类感知的极限了如指掌
Susan Barry knows all too well the limits of human perception.

37
00:02:38,350 --> 00:02:43,010
她出生就患有严重的斗鸡眼
She was born with her eyes severely crossed.

38
00:02:43,120 --> 00:02:45,110
婴儿时代 她的大脑企图
As a baby,her brain's attempts

39
00:02:45,230 --> 00:02:48,150
将分别从两只眼睛中看到的独立的二维图像
to fuse the separate two-dimensional images

40
00:02:48,260 --> 00:02:53,660
融合成一个三维图像 遇到了严重的困难
from each eye into one 3-D image ran into serious trouble.

41
00:02:53,770 --> 00:02:56,890
我小时候 是个斗鸡眼
Now,when I was little,being cross-eyed,

42
00:02:57,010 --> 00:03:00,230
如果我 比方说 用右眼看这个苹果
if I,let's say,looked at the apple with my right eye,

43
00:03:00,240 --> 00:03:02,740
我的左眼就会转过去看别的东西 -
my left eye would be turned in and looking at something else --

44
00:03:02,760 --> 00:03:05,660
比如这个钟
let's say, this clock.

45
00:03:06,480 --> 00:03:09,270
这样就意味着一只眼睛在看钟
So that would mean one eye is seeing the clock

46
00:03:09,390 --> 00:03:11,240
一只眼睛在看苹果
and one eye is seeing the apple,

47
00:03:11,360 --> 00:03:13,380
大脑可能会将其解释成
and the brain might interpret that

48
00:03:13,490 --> 00:03:16,350
认为时钟和苹果
to think that the clock and the apple

49
00:03:16,460 --> 00:03:18,720
是在空间的同一个地方
were in the same place in space.

50
00:03:18,830 --> 00:03:22,190
现在 你若是如此认为的话 那可是一个站不住脚的情形啊
Now,if you think about that,that's an untenable situation.

51
00:03:22,300 --> 00:03:25,590
因为你怎么能够知道如何移动
Because how would you be able to know how to move

52
00:03:25,710 --> 00:03:27,030
并与东西互动
and interact with things

53
00:03:27,140 --> 00:03:29,530
若是你不知道它们的空间位置的话？
if you don't know where they are in space?

54
00:03:29,640 --> 00:03:31,600
所以 如果你的眼睛那样斗鸡的话
So,if your eyes are crossed like that,

55
00:03:31,710 --> 00:03:33,200
你得找到办法去适应
you have to find a way to adapt,

56
00:03:33,310 --> 00:03:36,100
有个适应之道 我用过的
and one way to adapt,the way that I used,

57
00:03:36,220 --> 00:03:38,410
只不过就是抛弃一只眼睛看到的信息
was I simply threw out the information from one eye,

58
00:03:38,520 --> 00:03:39,710
那只看别处的眼睛
the eye that was turned.

59
00:03:39,820 --> 00:03:43,110
弗里曼：苏珊小时候做了眼科手术
Susan had eye surgeries when she was a child,

60
00:03:43,220 --> 00:03:45,580
但手术只是改变了她的外表
but they only changed her outward appearance.

61
00:03:45,690 --> 00:03:48,350
她只能看到两个维度
She could only see two dimensions.

62
00:03:48,460 --> 00:03:50,190
没有什么东西是有深度的
Nothing had any depth.

63
00:03:50,300 --> 00:03:53,220
所有一切 甚至她自己的镜像
Everything,even her own reflection,

64
00:03:53,340 --> 00:03:56,130
看上去完全就是平平的
looked entirely flat.

65
00:03:56,240 --> 00:04:00,700
似乎她的生活永远就是那个样子了
And it seemed she would live that way forever.

66
00:04:00,810 --> 00:04:05,070
过去半个世纪里 一直有个信条
For the past half century,there has been a belief

67
00:04:05,180 --> 00:04:10,170
就是如果你在襁褓期没有培育出
that if you did not develop the ability to see in 3-D

68
00:04:10,290 --> 00:04:12,880
立体观察的能力的话
within the first years of life in early childhood,

69
00:04:12,990 --> 00:04:15,550
你到了成年也不会培育出来的
you could not develop it as an adult.

70
00:04:15,660 --> 00:04:18,450
弗里曼：然而就在她近50岁的时候
But in her late 40s,

71
00:04:18,560 --> 00:04:22,190
苏珊开始了严格的视力在培训计划
Susan began a rigorous vision retraining program

72
00:04:22,300 --> 00:04:26,020
尝试教会她的眼睛锁定同一个目标
to try to teach her eyes to lock onto the same target

73
00:04:26,140 --> 00:04:28,230
让她的大脑有机会发现
and give her brain the chance to discover

74
00:04:28,340 --> 00:04:30,830
空间其它的维度
an extra dimension of space.

75
00:04:30,940 --> 00:04:34,630
有一天 在她48岁生日过后
One day,after her 48th birthday,

76
00:04:34,750 --> 00:04:37,840
奇迹发生了
something incredible happened.

77
00:04:37,950 --> 00:04:40,970
巴里：我走向自己的汽车 坐在驾驶座上
I went out to my car and I sat down in the driver's seat,

78
00:04:41,090 --> 00:04:43,140
我看向方向盘
and I went to look at the steering wheel,

79
00:04:43,260 --> 00:04:45,780
它突了出来
and it had popped out.

80
00:04:45,890 --> 00:04:49,680
这个空间一清二楚地突出在
It was popped out in space with this palpable pocket of space

81
00:04:49,790 --> 00:04:52,720
方向盘与仪表盘之间
between the steering wheel and the dashboard.

82
00:04:52,830 --> 00:04:55,420
我从未见到过那样的东西
And I had never seen anything like that.

83
00:04:55,530 --> 00:04:58,960
那一整天 我的立体视觉的出现
And all that day,my stereo vision would emerge

84
00:04:59,070 --> 00:05:01,090
是间歇性的 出乎意料的
like intermittently,unexpectedly,

85
00:05:01,210 --> 00:05:03,190
让人震惊
and it would be amazing.

86
00:05:03,310 --> 00:05:07,570
水龙头就突出在我的面前
The sink faucets were really jutting out toward me,

87
00:05:07,680 --> 00:05:11,000
我记得边兴赏水龙头
and I can remember just admiring the sink faucets

88
00:05:11,120 --> 00:05:14,370
边思忖我从未见过有弧形
and thinking that I had never seen an arc

89
00:05:14,490 --> 00:05:18,110
如这些水龙头那样美丽的弧形
as beautiful as the arc of those sink faucets.

90
00:05:18,220 --> 00:05:21,150
弗里曼：这额外的维度的突然现身
The sudden appearance of this extra dimension

91
00:05:21,260 --> 00:05:24,050
是苏珊.巴里的一个启示
was a revelation to Susan Barry.

92
00:05:24,160 --> 00:05:27,120
但是我们所知晓的三维之外
But the idea that another dimension

93
00:05:27,230 --> 00:05:29,120
有另一个维度
beyond the three we know

94
00:05:29,230 --> 00:05:32,690
可能隐藏着不为我们大家发现的概念
might be hiding from all of us is now at the center

95
00:05:32,800 --> 00:05:36,560
现在成了世界上最重要的科学调查的关注点
of the world's most important scientific investigations.

96
00:05:36,670 --> 00:05:40,930
哈佛大学物理学教授丽莎.兰德尔
Harvard Professor of physics Lisa Randall

97
00:05:41,040 --> 00:05:43,570
处在这场搜寻的前列
is at the forefront of this hunt.

98
00:05:43,680 --> 00:05:47,170
她看到的世界与你我不同
She sees the world differently from you and me.

99
00:05:47,280 --> 00:05:49,340
兰德尔：就有那么一天 我走着去上班
It was just one day I was walking to work,

100
00:05:49,450 --> 00:05:51,400
我意识到我确实觉得有额外的维度
and I realized I really did think that extra dimensions

101
00:05:51,510 --> 00:05:52,510
可能就存在着
could be out there.

102
00:05:52,630 --> 00:05:54,780
弗里曼：她坚信必定存在有
The main reason for her conviction

103
00:05:54,890 --> 00:05:57,520
不止三个维度的主要原因是什么？
that there must be more than three dimensions?

104
00:05:59,260 --> 00:06:01,950
这个回形针
This paperclip.

105
00:06:02,060 --> 00:06:03,490
它确实很奇怪
It's really strange.

106
00:06:03,600 --> 00:06:07,520
如果我拿起这块小磁铁 我就可以拿起这个回形针
If I take this tiny magnet,I can pick up this paperclip

107
00:06:07,640 --> 00:06:11,860
哪怕整个地球在往下拉这个回形针
even though the entire Earth is pulling down on this paperclip.

108
00:06:11,970 --> 00:06:14,100
你不妨想想 那磁力
If you think about it,the force of magnetism

109
00:06:14,210 --> 00:06:17,530
施加给这个回形针上的 足以匹敌
that is exerted on this paperclip is enough to compete

110
00:06:17,650 --> 00:06:21,470
实际上是胜过了作用于它的引力
and actually overwhelm the force of gravity that's acting on it.

111
00:06:21,580 --> 00:06:23,470
所以说其中有奥秘存在
So there's a mystery there,

112
00:06:23,590 --> 00:06:27,010
因为为什么电磁力能如此强大到
because why is electromagnetism so much stronger

113
00:06:27,120 --> 00:06:28,810
超过引力呢？
than the force of gravity?

114
00:06:28,930 --> 00:06:31,680
弗里曼：物理学家已经发现
Physicists have discovered

115
00:06:31,800 --> 00:06:35,390
我们所在的世界由四种基本力量控制
that we live in a world governed by four primal forces.

116
00:06:35,500 --> 00:06:37,660
有电磁力
There is electromagnetism,

117
00:06:37,770 --> 00:06:41,430
该力作用于带电荷的物体…
the force that affects objects with electric charge...

118
00:06:41,540 --> 00:06:43,230
强核力
The strong nuclear force,

119
00:06:43,340 --> 00:06:46,430
其能量在核弹里释放出来
whose power is unleashed in nuclear weapons,

120
00:06:46,540 --> 00:06:50,200
以及引发放射性衰变的弱核力
and the weak nuclear force that triggers radioactive decay.

121
00:06:50,310 --> 00:06:54,840
这三种力大致旗鼓相当
These first three forces are all roughly equal in strength.

122
00:06:54,950 --> 00:06:58,180
然而第四种力 引力 则要弱很多
But the fourth force,gravity,is much weaker.

123
00:06:58,290 --> 00:07:03,350
事实上 它要比另外三种力
In fact,it's around a trillion,trillion,trillion times

124
00:07:03,460 --> 00:07:06,050
还要弱兆兆兆倍
weaker than the other three.

125
00:07:06,160 --> 00:07:10,120
因此我们正努力搞明白怎样去解释引力为何
So we're trying to understand what can explain why gravity

126
00:07:10,230 --> 00:07:12,860
远弱于其它基本力
is so much weaker than the other elementary forces.

127
00:07:12,970 --> 00:07:15,890
有一个可能性 是我们近一二十年里
And one of the possibilities that we start to think about

128
00:07:16,010 --> 00:07:18,260
非常认真考虑的
quite seriously in the last decade or two

129
00:07:18,380 --> 00:07:21,800
就是实际上可能存在有另外的空间维度
is that there could actually be additional dimensions of space.

130
00:07:21,910 --> 00:07:25,170
如果那是真的 有可能引力的微弱
If that's true,it could be that gravity's weak

131
00:07:25,280 --> 00:07:26,900
是因为它其实集中在了
because it's actually concentrated

132
00:07:27,020 --> 00:07:28,570
另一个维度的某个地方
somewhere else in another dimension.

133
00:07:28,690 --> 00:07:31,410
弗里曼：额外维度的想法
The idea that extra dimensions

134
00:07:31,520 --> 00:07:35,350
有可能是我们现实的隐藏部分 其可追溯到帕拉图
might be a hidden part of our reality is as old as Plato.

135
00:07:35,460 --> 00:07:37,980
他想象我们所在的世界
He imagined the world we live in

136
00:07:38,100 --> 00:07:41,550
就像是被火光照亮的洞穴岩壁
to be like the wall of a cave lit by firelight.

137
00:07:41,670 --> 00:07:44,760
魅影舞蹈掠过我们的二维世界
Shadows dance across our two-dimensional world

138
00:07:44,870 --> 00:07:47,630
那是洞穴里第三个维度的物体的投影
cast by objects in the body of the cave

139
00:07:47,740 --> 00:07:51,000
我们没看见
in a third dimension that's hidden from us.

140
00:07:51,110 --> 00:07:55,130
三维立体形状如四面体
A three-dimensional geometrical shape like the tetrahedron,

141
00:07:55,250 --> 00:07:56,870
它有四个等边
which has four equal sides,

142
00:07:56,980 --> 00:07:59,600
可以在岩壁上投射出一个扭曲的阴影
could cast a distorted shadow on the wall

143
00:07:59,720 --> 00:08:04,440
以至于一边看上去比其它边短很多
so that one side looks much shorter than the others.

144
00:08:04,560 --> 00:08:05,940
宛如一个额外的维度
Just as an extra dimension

145
00:08:06,060 --> 00:08:08,580
能够掩饰其中一条边的长度一样
can hide the true length of one of the sides,

146
00:08:08,690 --> 00:08:13,150
所以 同样 它有可能掩饰掉引力真正的强度
so,too,it might be hiding the true strength of gravity.

147
00:08:13,260 --> 00:08:16,660
丽莎.兰德尔认识额外维度的努力
And Lisa Randall's efforts to learn about extra dimensions

148
00:08:16,770 --> 00:08:22,290
始于 和柏拉图一样 研究阴影
begins,like Plato's,with studying shadows.

149
00:08:22,410 --> 00:08:24,230
这里我有一个三维的立方体
So here I have a three-dimensional cube.

150
00:08:24,340 --> 00:08:25,930
现在 我不妨来做一个投影
Now,if I had a single projection,

151
00:08:26,040 --> 00:08:27,430
实际上我可以来混淆一下
I might actually confuse that,

152
00:08:27,550 --> 00:08:29,370
比如 就是一个正方形
for example,of just being a square,

153
00:08:29,480 --> 00:08:30,640
那是二维的
which is two-dimensional.

154
00:08:30,750 --> 00:08:32,470
然而 转动物体
However,by rotating the object

155
00:08:32,580 --> 00:08:34,610
从不同的角度
and looking from different angles

156
00:08:34,720 --> 00:08:36,110
看到不同的投影
with different projections,

157
00:08:36,220 --> 00:08:38,410
你就可以说出你手里的是个三维的物体
you can tell that what you have is a three-dimensional object.

158
00:08:38,520 --> 00:08:40,250
将信息凑在一起
By putting together the information,

159
00:08:40,360 --> 00:08:41,610
你就可以推断出那有什么
you can deduce what's there.

160
00:08:41,730 --> 00:08:43,780
弗里曼：就像二维阴影
Just as a two-dimensional shadow

161
00:08:43,900 --> 00:08:47,520
可以帮助我们认识三维立方体的真实形状一样
can help us learn the true shape of a three-dimensional cube,

162
00:08:47,630 --> 00:08:50,960
我们可以探索四维立方体
we can explore a four-dimensional cube,

163
00:08:51,070 --> 00:08:54,630
超立方体 通过观察其三维阴影
a hypercube,by looking at its three-dimensional shadows.

164
00:08:54,740 --> 00:08:57,730
我们可以看到超立方体各个投影
We can look at different projections of a hypercube.

165
00:08:57,850 --> 00:08:58,970
我们会看到的
What we would see

166
00:08:59,080 --> 00:09:00,800
是从一个角度去看立方体那样的东西
are things from one angle that might look a cube.

167
00:09:00,910 --> 00:09:03,340
从另一个角度 它可能看上去就像是 立方体里面有个立方体
From other angles,it might look like a cube inside a cube.

168
00:09:03,450 --> 00:09:05,540
它可能看上去就像是自我从内往外翻转
It might look like it's turning itself inside out

169
00:09:05,650 --> 00:09:08,380
因为我们并不是真的在第四维里
because we're not really in the fourth dimension,

170
00:09:08,490 --> 00:09:11,640
因此它的举动是我们并不熟悉的
so it does things that we're not familiar with

171
00:09:11,760 --> 00:09:13,410
因为它具有这整个其它的空间维度
because it has this whole other dimension of space

172
00:09:13,530 --> 00:09:14,650
它可以表现出来
that it can play with.

173
00:09:14,760 --> 00:09:17,220
弗里曼：不过若是有第四维度的存在
But if a fourth dimension does exist,

174
00:09:17,330 --> 00:09:20,690
我们不会看到有物体如此变化形状
shouldn't we see objects changing shapes like this,

175
00:09:20,800 --> 00:09:23,460
甚至会自我由内往外翻转吧？
even turning themselves inside out?

176
00:09:23,570 --> 00:09:27,660
难道存在于第四维度里的东西
Could it be that whatever exists in the fourth dimension

177
00:09:27,770 --> 00:09:30,630
不知咋的被阻止进入我们的世界么？
is somehow blocked from entering our world?

178
00:09:30,740 --> 00:09:32,700
还是它们被某种方式隐匿起来了？
Or could they be hidden some other way?

179
00:09:32,810 --> 00:09:34,940
兰德尔：因此 若是有额外的维度
So,if there are extra dimensions,

180
00:09:35,050 --> 00:09:36,400
它们必定得很好地隐匿起来
they have to be pretty well-hidden

181
00:09:36,520 --> 00:09:37,570
让我们无法去发现它们
for us not to have seen them.

182
00:09:37,690 --> 00:09:39,170
那为何会是是这个样子？
So,why would that be?

183
00:09:39,290 --> 00:09:41,040
可能是这些其它的维度
It could be these other dimensions

184
00:09:41,160 --> 00:09:43,310
非常之小 我们只是发现不了它们
are just so tiny we just don't notice them.

185
00:09:43,420 --> 00:09:44,510
弗里曼：然而这位科学家
But this scientist

186
00:09:44,630 --> 00:09:47,480
认为他已经发现了新方法来察觉它们
thinks he's discovered a new way to detect them

187
00:09:47,600 --> 00:09:49,650
我们所无法看到的维度
and that dimensions we can't see

188
00:09:49,760 --> 00:09:53,170
控制着宇宙间万物运动的方式
control the way everything in the Universe moves.

189
00:09:57,650 --> 00:09:58,870
如果我们进入空间第四维度
What would it look like

190
00:09:58,980 --> 00:10:03,150
会是什么样子呢？
if we were to travel into a fourth dimension of space?

191
00:10:05,650 --> 00:10:07,510
这是很难想象的
It's not easy to imagine.

192
00:10:07,620 --> 00:10:10,380
不过这里有一个办法去得到概念
But here's one way to get an idea.

193
00:10:10,490 --> 00:10:15,120
把我的手掌看成是一个只有两个维度的世界
Think of the palm of my hand as a world of only two dimensions.

194
00:10:15,230 --> 00:10:19,290
如果有一个三维的球穿过它
If a three-dimensional ball were to pass through it,

195
00:10:19,410 --> 00:10:21,660
那我的手掌里的居民会看到什么？
what would the inhabitants of my palm see?

196
00:10:22,320 --> 00:10:25,480
一个圆圈在增大
A circle that grew

197
00:10:25,590 --> 00:10:29,100
然后收缩为一点 随后慢慢消失了
and then shrunk down to a dot before disappearing.

198
00:10:29,210 --> 00:10:33,170
所以 如果我可以走进第四维度
So,if I could move into the fourth dimension,

199
00:10:33,280 --> 00:10:37,840
我的三维投影就会变形 收缩
my three-dimensional projection would distort,shrink,

200
00:10:37,960 --> 00:10:43,020
最后消失在这个世界里 一片漆黑
and finally flicker out of this world,becoming totally dark.

201
00:10:46,160 --> 00:10:49,120
加州大学欧文分校的物理学家蒂姆.泰特
U.C. Irvine Physicist Tim Tait

202
00:10:49,230 --> 00:10:51,660
认为宇宙中多数物质
thinks most of the matter in the Universe

203
00:10:51,770 --> 00:10:55,430
或许已经进入了第四维度 变成了漆黑一团
may have moved into the fourth dimension and gone dark.

204
00:10:55,540 --> 00:10:59,030
他同时也花费了大部分时间
He,too,spends most of his time

205
00:10:59,150 --> 00:11:02,710
试图逃出平时束缚我们的维度
trying to escape the dimensions that normally confine us.

206
00:11:12,360 --> 00:11:13,450
泰特：你潜水时
When you scuba dive,

207
00:11:13,560 --> 00:11:15,420
你会马上意识到那样的事实
you become immediately aware of the fact

208
00:11:15,530 --> 00:11:17,420
你得控制你的高度
that you have to control how high you are,

209
00:11:17,530 --> 00:11:19,390
深度 要知道 你是在水里
how deep,you know,you are in the water,

210
00:11:19,500 --> 00:11:21,090
你距离水面有多近
how close you are to the surface,

211
00:11:21,200 --> 00:11:24,260
这样你就立马意识到实际上
and so you instantly become aware of the fact

212
00:11:24,370 --> 00:11:26,290
对于另一个维度
that there's another dimension

213
00:11:26,410 --> 00:11:28,630
某种程度你在实地是无法真正感受到的
in a way that you can't really feel when you're on the ground.

214
00:11:28,740 --> 00:11:31,630
弗里曼：蒂姆认为另一个维度
Tim believes that yet another dimension,

215
00:11:31,740 --> 00:11:33,930
第四维度 甚至有可能是
a fourth dimension,might be the key

216
00:11:34,050 --> 00:11:37,340
解释宇宙最深层的谜团之一的关键 -
to explaining one of the deepest mysteries of the Universe --

217
00:11:37,450 --> 00:11:40,640
暗物质之谜
the mystery of dark matter.

218
00:11:40,750 --> 00:11:44,010
近年来 我们已经真正意识到了事实上
In the recent years,we've become really aware of the fact

219
00:11:44,120 --> 00:11:46,180
我们在盘点我们宇宙的所有东西后
that when we account for all the stuff in our Universe,

220
00:11:46,290 --> 00:11:48,010
有东西不见了
there's stuff that's missing.

221
00:11:48,130 --> 00:11:51,450
我们可以看到它的引力吸引着其他东西
We can see it pulling on other things gravitationally,

222
00:11:51,560 --> 00:11:54,220
但除此之外 并没有留下任何存在的痕迹
but other than that,it doesn't leave any trace that it's there.

223
00:11:54,330 --> 00:11:58,290
弗里曼：科学家相信有暗物质的存在
Scientists are convinced dark matter exists

224
00:11:58,400 --> 00:12:02,460
因为它影响着恒星围绕星系的方式
because it's affecting the way stars rotate around galaxies.

225
00:12:02,580 --> 00:12:05,100
它的引力非常强大
The gravitational pull of it is so strong,

226
00:12:05,210 --> 00:12:07,200
他们估计暗物质
that they estimate dark matter

227
00:12:07,310 --> 00:12:11,100
比普通物质是5:1
outweighs normal matter by five to one.

228
00:12:11,220 --> 00:12:13,410
我们确实不知道暗物质是什么
We really don't know what dark matter is,

229
00:12:13,520 --> 00:12:15,990
但已有许多想法提了出来
but there have been many ideas that have been proposed

230
00:12:16,100 --> 00:12:17,100
试图去解释它
to try to explain it,

231
00:12:17,210 --> 00:12:19,750
我个人接受暗物质
and my own personal take on dark matter

232
00:12:19,860 --> 00:12:21,590
是关于额外维度的理论
is a theory with extra dimensions.

233
00:12:23,600 --> 00:12:27,590
弗里曼：蒂姆的想法是暗物质可能是
Tim's idea is that dark matter could be evidence

234
00:12:27,700 --> 00:12:30,220
第四维度存在的证据
that a fourth dimension exists,

235
00:12:30,340 --> 00:12:33,660
那个维度我们几乎是看不见的
a dimension that is almost impossible for us to see.

236
00:12:33,770 --> 00:12:35,700
泰特：所以说额外维度可比作
So an analogy for the extra dimension

237
00:12:35,810 --> 00:12:37,830
是观察船只的锚索
would be looking at the anchor line of a boat.

238
00:12:37,940 --> 00:12:40,970
你看到绳索伸到远方 你看到绳索
When you look at the line from far away,you see a line.

239
00:12:41,080 --> 00:12:42,340
你看到又长又细的东西
You see a long,thin object,

240
00:12:42,450 --> 00:12:44,770
你没意识到它其实是有宽度的
and you don't realize that it actually has width,

241
00:12:44,890 --> 00:12:47,140
它具有另一个维度 你可以移动的
that it has an extra direction that you can move

242
00:12:47,250 --> 00:12:49,210
如果你坐在其表面的话
if you were sitting on the surface of it.

243
00:12:49,320 --> 00:12:50,910
凑近一看 它实际上是个圆柱体
Close up,it's actually a cylinder.

244
00:12:51,030 --> 00:12:54,750
它很粗壮 你可以沿着它的外围移动
It's big and fat,and you can move around the periphery of it.

245
00:12:54,860 --> 00:12:58,450
弗里曼：如果粒子绕着这个圆柱移动
If particles are moving around this cylinder,

246
00:12:58,570 --> 00:13:00,390
如果它足够小的话
and if it were small enough,

247
00:13:00,500 --> 00:13:04,260
它们就会让我们看上去就好像它们根本没动一般
they would look to us like they were not moving at all.

248
00:13:04,370 --> 00:13:06,290
这就是我们关于额外维度的模型
So this is our model for an extra dimension.

249
00:13:06,410 --> 00:13:08,960
我们有这个浮子 它代表一个粒子
We have the Bob,which represents a particle.

250
00:13:09,080 --> 00:13:10,600
我旋转粒子
As I spin the particle around,

251
00:13:10,710 --> 00:13:13,800
它就会打圈 绳子将其保持在适当位置上
as it goes in a circle with the string holding it in place,

252
00:13:13,910 --> 00:13:16,270
那表示它在额外的维度里移动
and that represents it moving in the extra dimension.

253
00:13:16,380 --> 00:13:18,240
好 让我们来看看其如何动作
So,let's see how that works.

254
00:13:18,350 --> 00:13:21,040
现在我们看到它在额外的维度里打圈
So here we have it spinning around in the extra dimension.

255
00:13:21,160 --> 00:13:23,650
随着它越来越靠近 加速了起来
As it gets closer and closer,it speeds up.

256
00:13:23,760 --> 00:13:26,450
它速度越来越快 具有了更高的能量
It moves faster and faster and has more energy.

257
00:13:26,560 --> 00:13:29,050
尽管这个粒子看上去好像原地不动
Even though this particle looks like it's standing still,

258
00:13:29,160 --> 00:13:31,120
它可能实际上动作非常非常快
it could actually be moving very,very fast

259
00:13:31,230 --> 00:13:33,590
打着很小很小的圈子
just in a very,very small circle.

260
00:13:33,700 --> 00:13:36,530
弗里曼：运动中的任何粒子必须具有能量
Any particle that is moving must have energy,

261
00:13:36,640 --> 00:13:40,000
根据所有物理学里最著名的方程式
and according to the most famous equation in all physics,

262
00:13:40,110 --> 00:13:44,330
你具有了能量 你就具有了质量
if you have energy,you have mass.

263
00:13:44,450 --> 00:13:46,600
那就给了蒂姆灵光闪现
That gave Tim a flash of inspiration

264
00:13:46,720 --> 00:13:50,440
暗物质粒子实际上有可能是什么
about what dark-matter particles might actually be

265
00:13:50,550 --> 00:13:52,110
以及它们有可能引导我们
and how they might lead us

266
00:13:52,220 --> 00:13:54,510
发现第四维
to discovering the fourth dimension.

267
00:13:54,620 --> 00:13:56,550
泰特：光子是光的粒子
So photons are particles of light,

268
00:13:56,660 --> 00:13:59,950
但如果有另一个方向让光子可以穿行
but if there's another direction that photons can travel in,

269
00:14:00,060 --> 00:14:02,120
我们实际上就可以得到暗物质粒子了
we can actually get a dark-matter particle

270
00:14:02,230 --> 00:14:04,060
只要取上这些无质量的光子
by just taking these massless photons

271
00:14:04,170 --> 00:14:06,820
让它们在额外的维度里转圈就行了
and letting them move around in a circle in the extra dimension.

272
00:14:06,940 --> 00:14:08,630
弗里曼：若蒂姆是对的
If Tim's right,

273
00:14:08,740 --> 00:14:11,730
暗物质实际上是出自光
dark matter is actually made of light,

274
00:14:11,840 --> 00:14:14,600
无质量粒子呈现出具有质量
massless particles that appear to have mass

275
00:14:14,710 --> 00:14:16,800
因为它们竞相围绕着
because they are racing around

276
00:14:16,910 --> 00:14:21,270
微小的第四维度打圈 它太小了我们看不到
a tiny fourth-dimensional loop that's too small for us to see.

277
00:14:21,390 --> 00:14:22,940
但又是如何和何时
But how and when

278
00:14:23,050 --> 00:14:26,540
让这些光子离开我们的三维世界
did these photons leave our three-dimensional world

279
00:14:26,660 --> 00:14:29,080
进入到第四维度的呢？
and enter the fourth dimension?

280
00:14:29,190 --> 00:14:30,920
有个办法让你可以试着明白这个
One way you can try to understand this

281
00:14:31,030 --> 00:14:33,380
你不妨想想游乐场里有台旋转木马
is if you think about a round-about in a playground.

282
00:14:33,500 --> 00:14:36,220
它旋转得飞快
It's spinning around really fast.

283
00:14:36,330 --> 00:14:38,390
要登上旋转木马
Actually get onto the round-about,

284
00:14:38,500 --> 00:14:41,460
小孩跑动的速度得等同于
a child is gonna have to run around it at the same speed

285
00:14:41,570 --> 00:14:42,860
它旋转的速度
that it's spinning.

286
00:14:42,970 --> 00:14:46,330
但要是其旋转快于孩子的跑动
But if it's spinning faster than the child can actually run,

287
00:14:46,440 --> 00:14:50,060
那么就没有办法安全登录
then there's no way to get onto it safely.

288
00:14:50,180 --> 00:14:51,180
我们今天所看到的多数粒子
Most particles we have today

289
00:14:51,290 --> 00:14:52,570
恰恰就没有那么多的能量
just don't have that much energy.

290
00:14:52,680 --> 00:14:55,040
不过在宇宙很年轻时
But when the Universe was very young,

291
00:14:55,150 --> 00:14:57,610
它很小很热
it was very small and it was very hot.

292
00:14:57,720 --> 00:15:00,280
当时 粒子具有更多的能量
And at that time,particles had a lot more energy,

293
00:15:00,390 --> 00:15:03,380
它们就真正能够进入到额外的维度里去
and they were able to actually get into the extra dimension.

294
00:15:03,500 --> 00:15:05,690
弗里曼：就在大爆炸之后
Right after the Big Bang,

295
00:15:05,800 --> 00:15:08,060
光的超高能粒子
super high-energy particles of light

296
00:15:08,170 --> 00:15:11,360
可能就这样被炸进了第四维度
may have blasted their way into the fourth dimension.

297
00:15:11,470 --> 00:15:14,260
它们从此被套牢在了那里
They have been stuck there ever since

298
00:15:14,370 --> 00:15:18,400
今天呈现给我们的是暗物质
and appear to us today as dark matter.

299
00:15:18,510 --> 00:15:21,640
不过蒂姆认为可能有办法让它们出来
But Tim thinks there might be a way for them to get out,

300
00:15:21,750 --> 00:15:25,470
一旦它们这样做的话 就有可能给我们带来证明
and when they do,they could bring us proof

301
00:15:25,590 --> 00:15:29,910
第四维度确实存在
that the fourth dimension really exists.

302
00:15:30,020 --> 00:15:33,350
如果有两个光子以相对方向围绕着
If two photons are moving around this curled-up dimension

303
00:15:33,460 --> 00:15:34,780
这个卷曲的维度转动
in opposite directions,

304
00:15:34,900 --> 00:15:38,350
它们就有可能偶尔相撞在一起
they might occasionally bump into one another.

305
00:15:38,470 --> 00:15:42,030
它们相撞时 就会湮灭迸发成
When they collide,they annihilate and burst out

306
00:15:42,140 --> 00:15:47,200
一阵能量雨进入到我们的3-D宇宙里来
as an intense shower of energy into our 3-D Universe.

307
00:15:47,310 --> 00:15:49,370
尽管这一事件十分罕见
Even though this event is rare,

308
00:15:49,480 --> 00:15:52,340
但第四维里的这些碰撞
these collisions in the fourth dimension

309
00:15:52,450 --> 00:15:54,770
应该会产生警告讯号
should create a telltale signal.

310
00:15:54,890 --> 00:15:58,240
点火 升空
Engines start. Liftoff.

311
00:15:58,360 --> 00:16:02,680
弗里曼：2008年 美国航天局发射了费米太空望远镜
In 2008,NASA launched the Fermi Space Telescope,

312
00:16:02,790 --> 00:16:07,050
探测器旨在截获强烈的辐射 伽马射线
a probe designed to pick up the intense radiation,gamma rays,

313
00:16:07,160 --> 00:16:11,490
产生自恒星爆炸那样的宇宙灾难
created by cosmic cataclysms like exploding stars.

314
00:16:11,600 --> 00:16:15,560
但它也能侦测到暗物质光子彼此湮灭时
But it should also detect gamma rays from dark-matter photons

315
00:16:15,670 --> 00:16:18,460
所发出的伽马射线
as they annihilate one another.

316
00:16:18,580 --> 00:16:22,170
这样 随着它收集数据 我们就能了解到伽马射线空域
So,as it collects data,we understand the gamma-ray sky,

317
00:16:22,280 --> 00:16:24,270
我们就着手寻找暗物质有可能存在的地方
and we start to look for where the dark matter might be.

318
00:16:24,380 --> 00:16:27,640
弗里曼：费米已经发现了有大量的伽马射线
Fermi has already discovered a sea of gamma rays

319
00:16:27,750 --> 00:16:30,310
源自我们银河系的中心
emanating from the center of our galaxy.

320
00:16:30,420 --> 00:16:32,140
但是需要有更多的工作
But much more work is needed

321
00:16:32,260 --> 00:16:35,850
来证明这个讯号是来自第四维
to prove this signal is coming from the fourth dimension.

322
00:16:35,960 --> 00:16:38,520
泰特：如此明显 我希望明天我们就能宣布胜利
So obviously,I hope that tomorrow we declare victory

323
00:16:38,630 --> 00:16:39,850
去探索其它的维度
and explore the extra dimension.

324
00:16:39,960 --> 00:16:41,020
从另一方面
On the other hand,

325
00:16:41,130 --> 00:16:42,790
我并不知道我们究竟何时能发现它
I don't know exactly when we're gonna discover it.

326
00:16:42,900 --> 00:16:46,390
不过 我认为现在的前景要远好于
I think,though,the prospects today are much better

327
00:16:46,500 --> 00:16:47,740
它们的过去
than they have been in the past.

328
00:16:50,340 --> 00:16:53,230
弗里曼：费米望远镜将会继续收集
The Fermi Telescope will continue gathering evidence

329
00:16:53,340 --> 00:16:57,650
太空深处的证据 直到2015年前后
from the depths of space until around 2015.

330
00:17:00,020 --> 00:17:02,610
不过要证明存在有不止三个维度
But proof that there are more than three dimensions

331
00:17:02,720 --> 00:17:04,180
可能并不是那么遥远了
may not come from so far away.

332
00:17:04,290 --> 00:17:08,650
眼下人类有史以来所打造的最大的实验
Right now the biggest experiment mankind has ever built

333
00:17:08,760 --> 00:17:12,660
正在瑞士的阿尔卑斯山底下努力去发现它们
is trying to find them under the Swiss Alps.

334
00:17:18,770 --> 00:17:20,230
科学目标
The goal of science

335
00:17:20,340 --> 00:17:24,900
就是向我们揭示大自然最深层的运作
is to reveal to us the deepest workings of nature.

336
00:17:25,010 --> 00:17:30,440
科学尝试里没有什么比弦理论更加深入
And nothing in science attempts to go deeper than string theory.

337
00:17:30,550 --> 00:17:35,240
弦理论称物质的每一个粒子
String theory says that every single particle of matter

338
00:17:35,360 --> 00:17:36,810
宇宙中的能量
and energy in the Universe

339
00:17:36,920 --> 00:17:41,920
其实都是小小的 颤动的弦…
is actually a tiny,vibrating string...

340
00:17:42,030 --> 00:17:48,990
弦的颤动并不是在三个维度上 而是九个
A string that vibrates not in three dimensions,but in nine.

341
00:17:49,100 --> 00:17:53,530
若是弦理论是正确的 那空间的每一点
If string theory is right,at every point in space,

342
00:17:53,640 --> 00:17:59,100
都有六个额外的维度紧紧缠绕在一起
there are six extra dimensions curled up incredibly tight.

343
00:17:59,210 --> 00:18:00,670
这些看不见的维度
These hidden dimensions

344
00:18:00,780 --> 00:18:04,840
可以解决所有的物理奥秘
could solve all the mysteries of physics.

345
00:18:04,950 --> 00:18:09,050
但是有一个问题
But there's a problem.

346
00:18:09,160 --> 00:18:12,720
自弦理论在40多年前首次提出以来
Since string theory was first proposed over 40 years ago,

347
00:18:12,830 --> 00:18:17,730
并没有丝毫证据支持它
there's not a single shred of evidence to support it.

348
00:18:20,700 --> 00:18:24,360
数以千计的科学家在追寻证据
Thousands of scientists are on the hunt for that evidence.

349
00:18:24,470 --> 00:18:27,400
日内瓦的阿尔卑斯山麓下
Under the foothills of the Alps in Geneva

350
00:18:27,510 --> 00:18:33,100
建有大型强子对撞机 即LHC
lies the Large Hadron Collider,the LHC.

351
00:18:33,210 --> 00:18:36,100
那是个17英里长的环形跑道
It's a 17-mile-long circular racetrack

352
00:18:36,220 --> 00:18:39,640
旨在将亚原子粒子撞击在一起
designed to smash subatomic particles together

353
00:18:39,750 --> 00:18:42,510
依靠惊人的能量
at phenomenal energies.

354
00:18:42,630 --> 00:18:46,120
加州理工学院的物理学教授玛利亚.丝波罗普鲁
Caltech Physics Professor Maria Spiropulu

355
00:18:46,230 --> 00:18:49,020
自大学毕业以后就一直在日内瓦
has been working at the atom smashers in Geneva

356
00:18:49,130 --> 00:18:51,690
从事粒子加速器工作
since she was an undergraduate.

357
00:18:51,800 --> 00:18:54,730
她见过无数粒子的飞行
She has seen trillions of particles fly

358
00:18:54,840 --> 00:18:58,340
如亚原子弹片那样穿过探测器
like subatomic shrapnel through the detectors.

359
00:19:00,440 --> 00:19:03,670
LHC 我觉得是人类所尝试过的最具雄心
The LHC,I think,is the most ambitious

360
00:19:03,780 --> 00:19:07,470
技术上最为复杂的科学项目
and technologically complex scientific project

361
00:19:07,590 --> 00:19:09,570
人类已经尝试过了
that humanity has ever attempted.

362
00:19:09,690 --> 00:19:11,980
我们每秒有10亿次碰撞
We got a billion collisions per second,

363
00:19:12,090 --> 00:19:15,710
记录这个数据可谓是项艰巨的任务
and this is a daunting task to record this data.

364
00:19:15,830 --> 00:19:18,920
弗里曼：玛利亚和她的同事筛选了
Maria and her colleagues have sifted through

365
00:19:19,030 --> 00:19:20,720
这一大堆数据
this immense pile of data

366
00:19:20,830 --> 00:19:24,260
甄别出了几十个亚原子粒子
and identified dozens of tiny subatomic particles,

367
00:19:24,370 --> 00:19:26,660
物质的基本模块
the basic building blocks of matter.

368
00:19:26,770 --> 00:19:28,990
但他们从未见到过
But they've never seen the strings

369
00:19:29,110 --> 00:19:32,100
深居在这些粒子中心的弦
that lie at the heart of each of these particles.

370
00:19:32,210 --> 00:19:35,500
弦理论预测它们必定
String theory predicts that they must be

371
00:19:35,610 --> 00:19:39,770
比原子要小上万亿 万亿倍
a trillion,trillion times smaller than an atom.

372
00:19:39,880 --> 00:19:41,340
换句话说 -
Put that another way --

373
00:19:41,450 --> 00:19:43,810
若是原子的大小相当于太阳系
if an atom were the size of the solar system,

374
00:19:43,920 --> 00:19:48,680
一个弦就相当于一个灯泡的大小
a string would be the size of a light bulb.

375
00:19:48,790 --> 00:19:50,550
目标越小
And the smaller an object is,

376
00:19:50,660 --> 00:19:54,080
则看到它所需的能量就越大
the more energy it takes to see it.

377
00:19:54,200 --> 00:19:57,890
环绕LHC飞行的亚原子粒子的能量
The energy of the subatomic particles racing around the LHC

378
00:19:58,000 --> 00:19:59,860
大得惊人
is staggeringly large.

379
00:19:59,970 --> 00:20:04,690
质子穿梭在这个环里飞快 乃至光束
Protons zip around this ring so fast that a beam of light

380
00:20:04,810 --> 00:20:08,800
也只能超越它们每小时约8英里
only outruns them by about eight miles an hour.

381
00:20:08,910 --> 00:20:10,740
但要看到基本的弦
But to see fundamental strings

382
00:20:10,850 --> 00:20:13,100
以及它们六个缠绕在一起的维度
and their six curled-up dimensions

383
00:20:13,220 --> 00:20:19,340
所需的能量几乎不可理喻
requires levels of energy almost beyond comprehension.

384
00:20:19,460 --> 00:20:21,810
丝波罗普鲁：如果你想做出一个对撞机
If you want to make a collider

385
00:20:21,930 --> 00:20:25,950
使其真正产生弦那样的东西
that will actually produce something like strings,

386
00:20:26,060 --> 00:20:29,320
所需的加速器要远大于LHC
it would take an accelerator much bigger than the LHC,

387
00:20:29,430 --> 00:20:32,720
远大过地球 地球的周长
much bigger than the Earth,the circumference of the Earth,

388
00:20:32,830 --> 00:20:35,330
没准远大过银河系
possibly much bigger than the Milky Way.

389
00:20:49,120 --> 00:20:52,080
弗里曼：不过或许有办法来证明弦理论
But there may be a way to prove that string theory

390
00:20:52,190 --> 00:20:55,950
以及伴随它的六个额外的空间维度
and the six extra dimensions of space that come with it

391
00:20:56,060 --> 00:20:57,420
是正确的
is correct,

392
00:20:57,530 --> 00:21:00,920
一个并不需要直接看到微小的弦的办法
a way that does not require seeing tiny strings directly.

393
00:21:01,030 --> 00:21:03,850
乔.泡钦斯基是世界上
Joe Polchinski is one of the world's

394
00:21:03,970 --> 00:21:05,790
首席弦理论家之一
leading string theorists.

395
00:21:05,900 --> 00:21:07,260
和许多物理学家一样
Like many physicists,

396
00:21:07,370 --> 00:21:10,530
他走进大自然以获得灵感
he draws inspiration from being close to nature.

397
00:21:10,640 --> 00:21:13,830
真是太棒了 走出去来到大自然来到山区
It's great to get out here in nature in the mountains

398
00:21:13,940 --> 00:21:16,470
来做一点思考
to think about things a bit.

399
00:21:16,580 --> 00:21:19,000
你登上高处
When you get to the top of a climb,

400
00:21:19,120 --> 00:21:22,870
你就会豁然开朗
you really get a much bigger picture.

401
00:21:22,990 --> 00:21:24,480
弗里曼：乔或许
Joe has probably

402
00:21:24,590 --> 00:21:27,540
更深入地探究弦理论的原理
delved deeper into the workings of string theory

403
00:21:27,660 --> 00:21:31,750
甚于其它任何人 在此过程中 他意识到
than anyone else,and in doing so,he realized

404
00:21:31,860 --> 00:21:35,290
有关键的东西消失在了数学中
something crucial was missing from the math.

405
00:21:35,400 --> 00:21:38,060
我们知道大自然的基本模块必定是
So,we know that the basic building blocks of nature

406
00:21:38,170 --> 00:21:39,260
很小很小的
have to be really small,

407
00:21:39,370 --> 00:21:41,290
小于我们所见过的任何东西 -
smaller than anything we've ever seen --

408
00:21:41,410 --> 00:21:42,690
或许是相当地小
probably a whole lot smaller.

409
00:21:42,810 --> 00:21:45,140
因此 如果这些模块是弦的话 那么要知道
So,if these building blocks are strings,you know,

410
00:21:45,250 --> 00:21:46,250
它们是难以捉摸的
they're very elusive.

411
00:21:46,370 --> 00:21:48,470
我们怎么知道它们的存在呢？
How do we know that they're there?

412
00:21:48,580 --> 00:21:51,140
所以说它极具挑战
And so it's challenging.

413
00:21:51,250 --> 00:21:53,570
我们曾做过一个计算
And there was this one calculation we would do,

414
00:21:53,680 --> 00:21:56,570
数学给我们的答案
and the answer that the math was giving us

415
00:21:56,690 --> 00:21:59,040
并没有匹配我们曾以为的
wouldn't match up with the physical picture

416
00:21:59,150 --> 00:22:00,150
物理图像
we thought we had.

417
00:22:00,260 --> 00:22:02,150
原来问题在于
It turned out that the problem was

418
00:22:02,260 --> 00:22:04,420
弦本身并不充分
the strings themselves were not enough.

419
00:22:04,530 --> 00:22:08,120
数学告诉我们的是有另一种东西
What the math was telling us was there was another kind of thing,

420
00:22:08,230 --> 00:22:10,220
有另一种对象在图像中
another sort of object in the picture.

421
00:22:10,340 --> 00:22:14,390
弗里曼：1995年 经过多年工作后
In 1995,after many years of work,

422
00:22:14,510 --> 00:22:17,330
乔以自己的方式通过恼人的数学
Joe made his way through the torturous math

423
00:22:17,440 --> 00:22:20,770
发现了弦的源头
and discovered the source of strings.

424
00:22:20,880 --> 00:22:25,600
他称这些东西为缔膜（D-Branes）
He called these objects D-branes.

425
00:22:25,720 --> 00:22:28,670
我们大老远远足到这里
So we're out here on this nice hike out here in nature,

426
00:22:28,790 --> 00:22:31,640
我们看到了这个漂亮的蜘蛛网
and we've got this beautiful spider web,

427
00:22:31,760 --> 00:22:34,110
这是某些概念的一个很好的模型
which is a nice model for some of these ideas.

428
00:22:34,230 --> 00:22:36,950
所以说缔膜是这些高维对象
So D-branes are these higher-dimensional objects.

429
00:22:37,060 --> 00:22:39,890
它们可以使二维的 三维的 甚至更多维的
They can be two-dimensional,three-dimensional,or even more.

430
00:22:40,000 --> 00:22:42,550
这个蜘蛛网是二维的 一张薄片
And this spider web is two-dimensional,a sheet,

431
00:22:42,670 --> 00:22:44,990
就像一张纸 它可以伸缩弯曲
and like a sheet,it can flex and bend

432
00:22:45,100 --> 00:22:47,260
同样蒂膜也可以伸缩弯曲
the way D-branes can flex and bend.

433
00:22:47,370 --> 00:22:48,630
现在 这并不是理想的模型
Now,it's not a perfect model

434
00:22:48,740 --> 00:22:51,100
因为这张网粘在了两根树枝之间
because this web is stuck between these two branches,

435
00:22:51,210 --> 00:22:53,170
然而蒂膜却可以延伸无尽头
but the D-branes can go on forever.

436
00:22:53,280 --> 00:22:54,770
它们可以是宇宙规模
They could be of cosmic size,

437
00:22:54,880 --> 00:22:57,600
从宇宙的一侧一直延伸到另一侧
stretching from one side of the Universe to another.

438
00:22:57,720 --> 00:22:58,940
你不妨仔细看看
And if you look close,

439
00:22:59,050 --> 00:23:01,670
你可以看到有小虫子粘在上面
you see that there are these little bugs stuck to it

440
00:23:01,790 --> 00:23:03,910
同样弦也粘在蒂膜上
the way strings get stuck to a D-brane.

441
00:23:04,020 --> 00:23:08,450
弗里曼：在乔的理论里 蒂膜可以取上
In Joe's theory,D-branes could take on

442
00:23:08,560 --> 00:23:10,010
九个维度中的任何维度
any of the nine dimensions

443
00:23:10,130 --> 00:23:13,520
这些维度存在于弦理论的数学中
that exist in the mathematics of string theory.

444
00:23:13,630 --> 00:23:17,150
我们整个宇宙可以是三维的膜
Our entire Universe could be a three-dimensional brane,

445
00:23:17,270 --> 00:23:19,960
大块的空间全都是弦
a block of space to which all the strings,

446
00:23:20,070 --> 00:23:24,830
我们宇宙中的物质都粘在上面
all the matter in our Universe is stuck.

447
00:23:24,940 --> 00:23:27,760
现在你看到了膜的作用
Now you have the branes doing what they do,

448
00:23:27,880 --> 00:23:29,700
你会发现极有可能
and you find that very possibly

449
00:23:29,810 --> 00:23:33,300
维度可能远远大于我们的想象
the dimensions could be much larger than we thought about,

450
00:23:33,420 --> 00:23:36,810
大得足以看到 粒子加速器
large enough to see particle accelerators,

451
00:23:36,920 --> 00:23:40,210
大得足以可以让我们看到其效果
large enough to maybe have effects on what we see

452
00:23:40,320 --> 00:23:43,330
在天体物理学里 在某些我们从太空中所看到的物理学里
in astrophysics,in some of the physics we see from space.

453
00:23:49,230 --> 00:23:51,020
弗里曼：多亏了乔的发现
Thanks to Joe's discovery,

454
00:23:51,140 --> 00:23:54,060
全世界的科学家充满了新的希望
scientists around the world are fueled with fresh hope

455
00:23:54,170 --> 00:23:59,170
他们可能很快就能发现额外的维度
that they may soon detect extra dimensions.

456
00:23:59,280 --> 00:24:05,200
如果你我 所有的星星 宇宙间所有的星系
If you,me,every star,every galaxy in the cosmos

457
00:24:05,320 --> 00:24:08,040
都是粘在三维的膜上的话
is stuck on a three-dimensional brane,

458
00:24:08,150 --> 00:24:09,340
那么第四维度
then a fourth dimension

459
00:24:09,450 --> 00:24:11,980
就不必是原子的一小部分了
wouldn't have to be a tiny fraction of an atom.

460
00:24:12,090 --> 00:24:15,380
它可要大多了
It could be much bigger.

461
00:24:15,490 --> 00:24:17,620
发现额外的维度
The discovery of extra dimensions

462
00:24:17,730 --> 00:24:20,190
将是科学史上
would be one of the biggest breakthroughs

463
00:24:20,300 --> 00:24:21,790
最大的突破之一
in the history of science.

464
00:24:21,900 --> 00:24:24,860
但它也可能带来灾祸
But it might also spell disaster.

465
00:24:24,970 --> 00:24:29,460
因为证明它们存在的实验
Because the experiment that proves they exist

466
00:24:29,580 --> 00:24:34,250
也可能会创造出地球上的黑洞
might also create a black hole here on Earth.

467
00:24:36,320 --> 00:24:40,440
1609年 伽利略透过他的望远镜
In 1609,Galileo peered through his telescope

468
00:24:40,550 --> 00:24:44,880
窥视到了木星的卫星
and spied the moons of Jupiter.

469
00:24:44,990 --> 00:24:47,950
他发现了那四个小小的光点
His discovery of those four tiny points of light,

470
00:24:48,060 --> 00:24:50,320
肉眼看不见
invisible to the naked eye,

471
00:24:50,590 --> 00:24:54,980
从而改变了我们对自己的世界的理解
changed our understanding of our world.

472
00:24:55,210 --> 00:24:56,730
额外的空间维度
Extra dimensions of space

473
00:24:56,840 --> 00:24:59,860
将远比伽利略的卫星更难看到
will be much harder to see than Galileo's moons,

474
00:24:59,980 --> 00:25:04,470
但一旦我们发现它们的话 那将改变我们
but if we discover them,it will change our understanding

475
00:25:04,580 --> 00:25:08,270
对整个宇宙的理解
of the entire Universe.

476
00:25:08,390 --> 00:25:10,280
这件精妙的平衡设备
This piece of delicately balanced equipment

477
00:25:10,390 --> 00:25:13,910
有可能是发现第四维的装置
could be the device that discovers the fourth dimension.

478
00:25:14,030 --> 00:25:18,280
它位于华盛顿大学的地下室
It sits in a basement at the University of Washington

479
00:25:18,400 --> 00:25:20,220
属于这个人的
and belongs to this man.

480
00:25:20,330 --> 00:25:23,520
埃里克.阿德尔伯格 与一个小组一道
Eric Adelberger,along with a small team,

481
00:25:23,630 --> 00:25:25,060
花了最近十年的时间
has spent the last decade

482
00:25:25,170 --> 00:25:28,590
来观察这台扭秤的来回扭动
watching this torsion balance twist back and forth,

483
00:25:28,710 --> 00:25:30,090
希望它能昭然若揭
hoping it reveals evidence

484
00:25:30,210 --> 00:25:34,260
证明存在超过三个以上的维度
that there are more than three dimensions.

485
00:25:34,380 --> 00:25:37,000
引力确实是个惊人的故事
Gravity is really an amazing story.

486
00:25:37,110 --> 00:25:39,200
它是物理学家所认识的
It was the first of the fundamental forces

487
00:25:39,310 --> 00:25:41,040
首个基本力
that the physicists learned about.

488
00:25:41,150 --> 00:25:43,670
牛顿有他的引力理论
Isaac Newton had his theory of gravity,

489
00:25:43,790 --> 00:25:47,010
它在太阳系里屡试不爽
which has been tested very well in the solar system.

490
00:25:47,120 --> 00:25:50,080
但它在很短的距离上的测试
But it's not really been tested very well at all

491
00:25:50,190 --> 00:25:51,650
非常不佳
at very short distances.

492
00:25:51,760 --> 00:25:52,810
短距离
And the short distances

493
00:25:52,930 --> 00:25:54,520
全都停留在理论上
are now where all the theoretical action is,

494
00:25:54,630 --> 00:25:55,830
可以这么说
so to speak.

495
00:25:57,660 --> 00:26:00,160
弗里曼：埃里克需要测量的力道
The forces Eric needs to measure

496
00:26:00,270 --> 00:26:01,460
极其微弱
are incredibly weak.

497
00:26:01,570 --> 00:26:03,660
尽管实验室在地下
Even though the lab is underground,

498
00:26:03,770 --> 00:26:07,500
但他的数据还是屡遭破坏 有交通高峰时刻的火车
his data is frequently marred by trains,rush-hour traffic,

499
00:26:07,610 --> 00:26:10,330
乃至高空飞行的飞机
even airplanes flying miles overhead.

500
00:26:10,440 --> 00:26:14,640
我们所测量的力道确实极其微小
The forces we're measuring are really extraordinarily tiny.

501
00:26:14,750 --> 00:26:18,710
为了有点概念 你不妨设法将一张邮票
To get some idea,if you could cut a postage stamp

502
00:26:18,820 --> 00:26:20,880
切成万亿小片
into a trillion little pieces somehow

503
00:26:20,990 --> 00:26:24,010
设法称重其中的一片
and could weigh one of those little pieces somehow,

504
00:26:24,130 --> 00:26:26,150
那种力道就是我们要测量的
that's the kind of forces that we're measuring.

505
00:26:26,260 --> 00:26:29,690
弗里曼：如果引力在很小的距离上偏离牛顿定律
If the force of gravity deviates from Newton's laws

506
00:26:29,800 --> 00:26:33,590
那将是一个警示信号
at very small distances,it would be a telltale sign

507
00:26:33,700 --> 00:26:36,930
有额外的微型维度存在
that an extra microscopic dimension exists.

508
00:26:37,040 --> 00:26:39,860
这是埃里克直接掌握的原则
It's a principle Eric knows firsthand

509
00:26:39,980 --> 00:26:42,230
来自他在实验室外的酷爱
from his passion outside the lab

510
00:26:42,350 --> 00:26:45,670
照料着另一套微妙的东西
tending another set of delicate objects.

511
00:26:45,780 --> 00:26:48,140
理解其的好方法就是这里的类比
A nice way to understand this is this analogy

512
00:26:48,250 --> 00:26:49,940
引力在不同维度间传播的方式
between the way gravity spreads out

513
00:26:50,050 --> 00:26:51,440
引力在不同维度间传播的方式
in varying number of dimensions

514
00:26:51,550 --> 00:26:53,110
与水流在不同维度间的流动方式
and the way flow of water spreads out

515
00:26:53,220 --> 00:26:54,590
与水流在不同维度间的流动方式
in varying number of dimensions.

516
00:26:56,630 --> 00:26:58,480
我们这里有一个源源不断地水流
We got a steady stream of water

517
00:26:58,590 --> 00:27:01,390
从顶部的两个口子流出
that flows out of these two outlets at the top,

518
00:27:01,500 --> 00:27:04,990
落在管道里 并被限制在一个维度里
and it falls into a channel and is confined in one dimension.

519
00:27:05,100 --> 00:27:07,060
它沿着一个维度流下
And it runs down along the one dimension,

520
00:27:07,170 --> 00:27:11,800
我们将一个管道乘以二 还有另一个管道
and we've made one channel twice as long as the other channel.

521
00:27:11,910 --> 00:27:13,900
我们将看到 - 测量水流
And we're gonna see -- measure the flow of water

522
00:27:14,010 --> 00:27:18,900
观察这个水桶相对这个水桶的
by watching how much the level of the water in this bucket

523
00:27:19,020 --> 00:27:22,940
水平面的变化情况 这里水流过的距离
changes compared to this bucket,where the water's had to travel

524
00:27:23,050 --> 00:27:25,320
得是那个维度里得两倍的距离
twice as far in that one dimension.

525
00:27:31,690 --> 00:27:33,220
流经较长一维管道的水量
The amount of water

526
00:27:33,330 --> 00:27:35,880
流经较长一维管道的水量
that's flowed through the longer one-dimensional channel

527
00:27:36,000 --> 00:27:37,950
完全等同于流经较短一维管道的水量
is just the same as the amount of water

528
00:27:38,070 --> 00:27:40,360
流经较短一维管道的水量
that's flowed through the shorter one-dimensional channel.

529
00:27:40,470 --> 00:27:43,530
所以这就告诉了我们有关引力的情况
So what this tells us about gravity is that if gravity

530
00:27:43,640 --> 00:27:46,530
即如果引力运作在一个维度的世界里
were operating in a one-dimensional world,

531
00:27:46,640 --> 00:27:49,530
不管物体靠的很近还是离得很远
it would be the same if objects are close together

532
00:27:49,650 --> 00:27:51,270
其都是一样的
or if they're very far apart.

533
00:27:51,380 --> 00:27:53,240
我们来看看水在两个维度里流动时
So now we're gonna see what happens

534
00:27:53,350 --> 00:27:55,080
所发生的情况
when the water flows in two dimensions.

535
00:28:10,170 --> 00:28:11,860
在我们的二维实验中
In our two-dimensional experiment,

536
00:28:11,970 --> 00:28:16,260
靠近水源的烧杯所得到的水是
the beaker that was closer to the water source

537
00:28:16,370 --> 00:28:17,930
离水源较远的烧杯的两倍多
got twice as much water

538
00:28:18,040 --> 00:28:20,660
离水源较远的烧杯的两倍多
as the beaker that was farther from the source.

539
00:28:20,780 --> 00:28:24,100
如果这两个烧杯就是我们对引力的计量
If these two beakers here were our measure of gravity,

540
00:28:24,210 --> 00:28:26,340
那么我们就能知道我们处在二维世界里
we would know that we were in a two-dimensional world

541
00:28:26,450 --> 00:28:30,120
因为我们在这里得到了两倍的水
because we got twice as much water over here.

542
00:28:32,050 --> 00:28:34,210
好 现在我们来看看水在三维世界里扩散时
Okay,now we're gonna see what happens

543
00:28:34,320 --> 00:28:36,690
所发生的情况
when the water spreads in three dimensions.

544
00:28:38,890 --> 00:28:42,050
弗里曼：水在三维世界里扩散时
When water spreads out in a three-dimensional world,

545
00:28:42,170 --> 00:28:45,360
你将烧杯安放靠近水源两倍
when you place the bucket twice as close to the source,

546
00:28:45,470 --> 00:28:48,540
你就能得到四倍多的水
you get four times as much water.

547
00:28:52,210 --> 00:28:54,630
我们不妨来罗列一下三个实验中的烧杯
So if we lined up the beakers from the three experiments,

548
00:28:54,750 --> 00:28:57,730
我们看到一维的烧杯 水量等同
we'd see that the 1-D beakers,the water was the same height,

549
00:28:57,850 --> 00:29:00,740
二维 就近的烧杯有两倍的水
2-D,the near beaker had twice the water,

550
00:29:00,850 --> 00:29:04,010
至于三维 就有了四倍的水
and in the case of 3-D,it had four times the water.

551
00:29:04,120 --> 00:29:07,640
现在 我们就可以想象我们生活在四维里
Now,if we could imagine that we were living in four dimensions,

552
00:29:07,760 --> 00:29:09,350
我们所看到的 我们预计会看到
what would we see,we would expect to see

553
00:29:09,460 --> 00:29:12,450
最近的烧杯的水量将会八倍于
that the nearer beaker had eight times the amount of water

554
00:29:12,560 --> 00:29:14,680
较远的烧杯里的水量
that the more distant one had.

555
00:29:14,800 --> 00:29:17,450
弗里曼：维度越多
The more dimensions there are,

556
00:29:17,570 --> 00:29:21,120
引力随距离的变化就越快
the faster the force of gravity changes with distance.

557
00:29:21,240 --> 00:29:26,760
我们已经测量了下至约50微米的引力
Well,we've measured gravity down to roughly 50 microns.

558
00:29:26,880 --> 00:29:29,970
那约是你头发直径的一半 懂么？
That's about half the diameter of a hair on your head,okay?

559
00:29:30,080 --> 00:29:34,910
至此 牛顿先生依然是正确的
So far,Mr. Isaac Newton is still correct.

560
00:29:35,020 --> 00:29:38,140
弗里曼：如果埃里克能够更进一步的话
If Eric can get even closer,

561
00:29:38,260 --> 00:29:40,710
那额外维度的隐蔽世界
the hidden world of extra dimensions

562
00:29:40,820 --> 00:29:42,380
将能够昭然若揭了
could suddenly pop into view.

563
00:29:42,490 --> 00:29:44,680
阿德尔伯格：有理由认为
There are reasons to think

564
00:29:44,800 --> 00:29:47,280
你知道 在50到10的范围内
that,you know,the region between 50 and 10

565
00:29:47,400 --> 00:29:49,220
有可能包含着某种惊喜 当然
might contain some real surprises,and,of course,

566
00:29:49,330 --> 00:29:52,860
那激励着我们做实验的热情
that's stimulating our enthusiasm

567
00:29:52,970 --> 00:29:54,440
做实验的热情
for doing the experiments.

568
00:29:56,370 --> 00:29:58,560
弗里曼：在地球的另一头
On the other side of the planet,

569
00:29:58,680 --> 00:30:00,700
在大型强子对撞机上
at the Large Hadron Collider,

570
00:30:00,810 --> 00:30:04,400
粒子物理学家玛利亚.丝波罗普鲁同样在寻找
Particle Physicist Maria Spiropulu is also looking

571
00:30:04,520 --> 00:30:08,240
出乎意料的引力变化.
for unexpected changes in the force of gravity.

572
00:30:08,350 --> 00:30:10,040
但要是她的实验取得成功
But if her experiment is successful,

573
00:30:10,160 --> 00:30:12,810
她将会创造出地球上从未见到过的东西 -
she'll create something never before seen on Earth --

574
00:30:12,930 --> 00:30:16,420
黑洞
a black hole.

575
00:30:16,530 --> 00:30:20,220
丝波罗普鲁：极有可能LHC实验
It is quite possible the LHC experiment

576
00:30:20,330 --> 00:30:23,790
会产生出所谓的微型黑洞
can produce the so-called microscopic black holes.

577
00:30:23,900 --> 00:30:26,730
弗里曼：这并非那种产生于塌缩星体的黑洞
This is not the type of black hole

578
00:30:26,840 --> 00:30:29,300
在那里塌缩的星核
that is borne from a collapsing star,

579
00:30:29,410 --> 00:30:31,300
被挤压得严严实实
where the core gets so compacted

580
00:30:31,410 --> 00:30:34,370
什么都无法摆脱其引力的作用
that nothing can escape its gravitational pull.

581
00:30:34,480 --> 00:30:36,470
玛利亚所要寻找的
What Maria is looking for

582
00:30:36,580 --> 00:30:40,140
是微型黑洞的证据
is evidence of a microscopic black hole.

583
00:30:40,250 --> 00:30:42,780
如果LHC能迫使两个粒子
If the LHC can force two particles

584
00:30:42,890 --> 00:30:44,810
充分靠拢在一起
sufficiently close together,

585
00:30:44,930 --> 00:30:48,120
额外维度足够大
and the extra dimensions are large enough,

586
00:30:48,230 --> 00:30:51,850
引力就可以逐渐增强 超过预期
gravity could start growing much stronger than expected,

587
00:30:51,970 --> 00:30:55,030
最终将两个粒子充分挤压
eventually compacting the two particles enough

588
00:30:55,140 --> 00:30:58,800
形成一个微型黑洞
to form a tiny subatomic black hole.

589
00:30:58,910 --> 00:31:02,870
但无用担心现在就迁移至火星
But don't worry about moving to Mars just yet.

590
00:31:02,980 --> 00:31:06,000
黑洞玛利亚及其同僚希望创造的
The black holes Maria and her colleagues expect to create

591
00:31:06,120 --> 00:31:08,200
是个小不点…
are tiny...

592
00:31:08,320 --> 00:31:12,050
小得它们会在若干分之一秒里就蒸发殆尽
So tiny that they will evaporate in a fraction of a second.

593
00:31:14,090 --> 00:31:17,380
微型黑洞 它们一旦产生
The microscopic black holes,as soon as they are produced,

594
00:31:17,490 --> 00:31:21,350
就会立刻衰变 寿命极短
they immediately decay with a very,very short life-span.

595
00:31:21,460 --> 00:31:25,760
会有一束粒子束 那就表明
There is a spray of these particles,and that is the clue

596
00:31:25,870 --> 00:31:28,930
那样一个对象有可能已经创造出来了
that such an object might have been created.

597
00:31:29,040 --> 00:31:33,100
弗里曼：LHC寻找这些黑洞
The LHC has been looking for these black holes

598
00:31:33,210 --> 00:31:34,530
已有一年多了
for over a year.

599
00:31:34,650 --> 00:31:37,270
迄今为止 他们并没有发现有
So far they found no hint

600
00:31:37,380 --> 00:31:40,440
黑洞创造出来的任何迹象
of even a single black hole being created.

601
00:31:40,550 --> 00:31:45,040
额外维度依然扑朔迷离
Extra dimensions remain elusive.

602
00:31:45,160 --> 00:31:47,810
但莉莎.蓝道尔认为那可能是
But Lisa Randall thinks that might be

603
00:31:47,930 --> 00:31:51,020
因为它们不同于大多数科学家所预期的东西
because they're different from what most scientists expect.

604
00:31:51,130 --> 00:31:54,590
她认为额外维度被扭曲了
She believes extra dimensions are warped

605
00:31:54,700 --> 00:31:59,100
它们是通向平行宇宙的通道
and that they are passageways to a parallel Universe.

606
00:32:01,900 --> 00:32:04,960
额外维度不易看到
Extra dimensions are not easy to see.

607
00:32:05,340 --> 00:32:09,660
如果它们在 我们早就发现它们了
If they were,we'd have found them long ago.

608
00:32:09,770 --> 00:32:11,300
许多科学家现在认为
Many scientists now believe

609
00:32:11,410 --> 00:32:14,030
我们将永远都不会有技术去发现它们
we'll never have the technology to find them.

610
00:32:14,350 --> 00:32:19,380
不过额外维度仍有可能自我暴露出来…
But extra dimensions might still reveal themselves...

611
00:32:19,490 --> 00:32:24,550
因为它们有可能正将我们从平行宇宙中分离出来
because they might be separating us from a parallel Universe.

612
00:32:24,660 --> 00:32:28,620
整个宇宙可能正蛰伏在
An entire cosmos could be lurking

613
00:32:28,730 --> 00:32:33,420
不足…万亿分之一英寸之间
less than...a trillionth of an inch away.

614
00:32:33,530 --> 00:32:35,860
哈佛大学教授莉莎.蓝道尔
Harvard Professor Lisa Randall

615
00:32:35,970 --> 00:32:39,730
有一个关于额外维度的激进新思路
has a radical new idea about extra dimensions,

616
00:32:39,840 --> 00:32:44,030
将会改变我们观察我们整个宇宙的看法
one that will change the way we see our entire Universe.

617
00:32:44,140 --> 00:32:46,970
她从弦理论着手
She began with string theory,

618
00:32:47,080 --> 00:32:50,340
就是那个概念 即所有的基本粒子
the idea that all the fundamental particles

619
00:32:50,450 --> 00:32:54,880
只不过是九维的弦的震颤而已
are just vibrations of tiny nine-dimensional strings.

620
00:32:54,990 --> 00:32:57,950
然后她加进了乔.泡钦斯基的想法
Then she added in Joe Polchinski's ideas

621
00:32:58,060 --> 00:33:01,220
就是构成我们宇宙间万物的弦
that strings making up all the stuff in our Universe

622
00:33:01,330 --> 00:33:04,820
必须粘接成巨大的三维物体
had to be stuck to a giant three-dimensional object

623
00:33:04,930 --> 00:33:07,220
即膜
called a brane.

624
00:33:07,340 --> 00:33:08,420
有两类弦 -
There are two types of strings --

625
00:33:08,540 --> 00:33:09,730
带有尾巴的弦
strings with ends

626
00:33:09,840 --> 00:33:12,760
以及闭合的弦 和橡皮筋那样
and strings that are closed loops,like rubber bands.

627
00:33:12,880 --> 00:33:15,670
带有尾巴的弦 其尾巴必定得在某个地方
And the strings with ends,those ends have to be somewhere.

628
00:33:15,780 --> 00:33:18,840
它们不能够呆在较高维度的空间里
They can't just be anywhere in higher-dimensional space.

629
00:33:18,950 --> 00:33:20,670
它们得呆在膜的表面
They have to be on the surface of a brane.

630
00:33:20,780 --> 00:33:21,870
若那是真的话
And if that's true,

631
00:33:21,990 --> 00:33:24,410
与那种弦有关的粒子
the particles associated with that string

632
00:33:24,520 --> 00:33:25,840
同样将在膜上
will also be on the brane.

633
00:33:25,960 --> 00:33:28,580
其结果就是我们所了解的物质
And it turns out that all the matter we know about,

634
00:33:28,690 --> 00:33:30,550
以及它们相互作用的力
and also the forces through which they interact,

635
00:33:30,660 --> 00:33:34,390
或许全都粘在这种构造所产生的膜上
might all be stuck on a brane through this mechanism,

636
00:33:34,500 --> 00:33:35,890
除了引力外
except for gravity.

637
00:33:36,000 --> 00:33:38,860
因为引力从不与开放的弦打交道
Because gravity is never associated with open string.

638
00:33:38,970 --> 00:33:41,330
引力与闭合的弦打交道
Gravity's associated with a closed string.

639
00:33:41,440 --> 00:33:42,960
闭合的弦没有尾巴
And closed strings have no ends.

640
00:33:43,070 --> 00:33:45,630
不存在使其粘在膜上的机制
There's no mechanism that makes it stick to a brane.

641
00:33:45,740 --> 00:33:47,640
闭合的弦可以在任何地方
A closed string can be anywhere.

642
00:33:53,750 --> 00:33:57,710
弗里曼：莉莎的计算提出引力有可能非常微弱
Lisa's math suggested that gravity might be so weak

643
00:33:57,820 --> 00:33:59,480
因为闭合的弦
because the closed-loop strings

644
00:33:59,590 --> 00:34:01,850
携带这种力 引力
that carry this force,gravitons,

645
00:34:01,960 --> 00:34:04,620
正把我们的膜拉开
are being pulled away from our brane

646
00:34:04,730 --> 00:34:07,580
而不是集中在一个平行宇宙中
and concentrated instead in a parallel Universe

647
00:34:07,700 --> 00:34:11,690
把我们从第四维里分离出来
that's separated from us by a fourth dimension.

648
00:34:11,800 --> 00:34:13,890
兰德尔：你可以想象我身后的这两栋大楼
You can imagine that these two buildings behind me

649
00:34:14,000 --> 00:34:15,990
代表两个不同的膜
represent two different branes,

650
00:34:16,110 --> 00:34:20,030
我们或许只生活在那栋大楼或那个膜里
and we maybe are living only in that building or that brane.

651
00:34:20,140 --> 00:34:22,230
如果引力集中在另外的大楼里
If gravity is concentrated at the other building,

652
00:34:22,350 --> 00:34:24,300
我们没准就只得到了引力的尾巴
we might only get a tail end of gravity.

653
00:34:24,410 --> 00:34:26,170
这或许能够解释
It might be that that could explain

654
00:34:26,280 --> 00:34:28,170
为何引力对我们如此微弱
why gravity is so weak for us.

655
00:34:28,280 --> 00:34:31,740
弗里曼：引力自由流动在我们的膜与
Gravitons flow freely between our brane

656
00:34:31,850 --> 00:34:34,540
跨越第四维的膜之间
and the one that's across the fourth dimension.

657
00:34:34,660 --> 00:34:38,180
但那个平行世界里的引力很强
But the gravity in that parallel world is so strong,

658
00:34:38,290 --> 00:34:39,580
它将空间压缩成我们世界的空间的
it compresses space

659
00:34:39,700 --> 00:34:43,120
万亿万亿倍小
trillions upon trillions of times smaller than ours.

660
00:34:43,230 --> 00:34:47,290
这两个膜世界之间的空间被扭曲了
The space between these two brane worlds is warped.

661
00:34:47,400 --> 00:34:48,760
在引力从致密引力的膜
As gravitons move

662
00:34:48,870 --> 00:34:51,400
传向我们的膜的过程中
from the dense-gravity brane to our brane,

663
00:34:51,510 --> 00:34:55,440
它们扩散了 其力道越来越微弱了
they spread out,and their force gets far weaker.

664
00:35:01,650 --> 00:35:02,940
东西得到了重整
Things get rescaled

665
00:35:03,050 --> 00:35:06,050
随着你从额外维度里的走入另一个维度
as you go from one place in an extra dimension to the other.

666
00:35:06,160 --> 00:35:08,710
所以东西在这里会非常重
So whereas things might be extremely heavy here,

667
00:35:08,830 --> 00:35:10,880
它们在这里会成倍成倍地轻
they could be exponentially lighter here,

668
00:35:11,000 --> 00:35:15,450
这就自然而然地解释了为什么引力会如此微弱
which would naturally explain why gravity is so weak.

669
00:35:15,570 --> 00:35:18,920
弗里曼：莉莎.蓝道尔的扭曲第四维的想法
Lisa Randall's idea of a warped fourth dimension

670
00:35:19,040 --> 00:35:21,090
把我们从平行宇宙里分离了出来
separating us from a parallel Universe,

671
00:35:21,200 --> 00:35:24,690
在那里引力和其它自然力是一样强的
where gravity is just as strong as the other forces of nature,

672
00:35:24,810 --> 00:35:28,610
引起了物理界的轰动
has set the world of physics alight.

673
00:35:36,750 --> 00:35:39,850
回到日内瓦的大型强子对撞机
Back at the Large Hadron Collider in Geneva,

674
00:35:39,960 --> 00:35:42,280
粒子束很快就会撞击在了一起
the beams will soon be smashing together

675
00:35:42,390 --> 00:35:44,620
有足够的力量来产生粒子
with enough force to produce particles

676
00:35:44,730 --> 00:35:49,620
那将会证明这个弯曲的维度的存在
that could prove this warped dimension really exists.

677
00:35:49,730 --> 00:35:52,720
蓝道尔：若这个想法是对的
Well,if this idea is right,

678
00:35:52,840 --> 00:35:55,260
你实际上就能让粒子
you would actually be able to make particles

679
00:35:55,370 --> 00:35:57,860
基本具有其它维度里的动能
that essentially have momentum in another dimension.

680
00:35:57,980 --> 00:35:59,930
现在 我们无法看到其它维度
Now,we don't see that other dimension.

681
00:36:00,040 --> 00:36:03,900
我们所看到的是效果 就好像粒子具有质量
What we see is the effect as if the particle had mass,

682
00:36:04,010 --> 00:36:06,070
这质量结果恰恰就是质量
and the mass turns out to be the right mass

683
00:36:06,180 --> 00:36:08,040
它能够产生于大型强子对撞机的能量中
that it can be produced at the energies

684
00:36:08,150 --> 00:36:10,120
但愿如此
of the Large Hadron Collider,we hope.

685
00:36:13,360 --> 00:36:17,310
弗里曼：现在任何一天 都或许会有新闻来自瑞士阿尔卑斯山
Any day now,news may come from the Swiss Alps

686
00:36:17,430 --> 00:36:19,580
世界根本不同于
that the world is fundamentally different

687
00:36:19,700 --> 00:36:21,690
我们一直以为的那样
from the way we've always imagined it.

688
00:36:21,800 --> 00:36:24,920
然而有一个更大的扭曲
But there is one more twist to this epic hunt

689
00:36:25,040 --> 00:36:28,290
针对这个扭曲或卷曲的维度的史诗般的搜寻
for warped or curled-up extra dimensions.

690
00:36:28,410 --> 00:36:33,100
有位科学家认为我们的搜索注定要失败的
One scientist thinks our search is doomed to failure.

691
00:36:33,210 --> 00:36:37,340
她并不相信存在有不止三个维度
She does not believe there are more than three dimensions.

692
00:36:37,450 --> 00:36:39,980
她认为只有一个
She thinks there's only one.

693
00:36:43,490 --> 00:36:46,630
你如何来构建宇宙呢？
How do you build a Universe?

694
00:36:46,750 --> 00:36:48,780
你需要三个维度么？
Do you need three dimensions?

695
00:36:48,900 --> 00:36:53,220
抑或你需要四个？ 九个？ 甚至更多？
Or do you need four? Nine? Or more?

696
00:36:53,480 --> 00:36:55,710
这些是科学家拷问我们
These are the most fundamental questions

697
00:36:55,820 --> 00:36:59,310
现实的最基本的问题
scientists can ask about our reality.

698
00:36:59,420 --> 00:37:04,260
然而最简单的问题通常都是最难回答的
But the simplest questions are often the hardest to answer.

699
00:37:06,650 --> 00:37:09,980
大型强子对撞机以及世界各地实验室里的
Swarms of scientists at the Large Hadron Collider

700
00:37:10,090 --> 00:37:11,450
成群的科学家
and labs around the world

701
00:37:11,560 --> 00:37:14,120
都在搜寻额外维度的证据
are hunting for evidence of extra dimensions,

702
00:37:14,230 --> 00:37:18,320
它们会弯曲或卷曲在小小的循环里
be they warped or curled up in tiny loops.

703
00:37:18,430 --> 00:37:20,820
他们希望在未来几年里
They hope to make a major breakthrough

704
00:37:20,940 --> 00:37:22,460
取得重大突破
within the next few years.

705
00:37:22,570 --> 00:37:27,630
但是雷娜塔.洛尔 乌得勒支大学的物理学家
But Renate Loll,a physicist at the University of Utrecht,

706
00:37:27,740 --> 00:37:28,960
并没有为之所动
isn't holding her breath.

707
00:37:29,080 --> 00:37:33,230
当然 你在弦理论里有一个问题
Of course,one of the problems you have in string theory

708
00:37:33,350 --> 00:37:36,140
那就是全都存在许多维度
is that there's all these many dimensions.

709
00:37:36,250 --> 00:37:41,170
然后你得解释为什么你只能看到其中的一些
Then you have to explain why you only see a few of them.

710
00:37:41,290 --> 00:37:43,810
你若能做到那将是很了不起的
That would be wonderful if you could do that.

711
00:37:43,920 --> 00:37:46,880
但是目前太困难了
But currently that's too difficult

712
00:37:46,990 --> 00:37:48,650
没人能够表明那一点
or no one has managed to show that.

713
00:37:48,760 --> 00:37:50,720
弗里曼：雷娜塔认为
Renate believes

714
00:37:50,830 --> 00:37:53,520
弦理论所预言的额外维度
that the extra dimensions predicted by string theory

715
00:37:53,630 --> 00:37:56,160
只不过是数学上的巧合
are merely a mathematical quirk

716
00:37:56,270 --> 00:38:00,660
理论本身可能就是错误的
and the theory itself is likely to be wrong.

717
00:38:00,770 --> 00:38:02,390
当然 它引发的问题是
Of course,it raises the question of,

718
00:38:02,510 --> 00:38:03,830
好 我们或许能够
"Well,can we maybe do

719
00:38:03,940 --> 00:38:06,600
不用这些额外的维度来做么？
without these extra dimensions whatsoever?"

720
00:38:06,710 --> 00:38:08,630
弗里曼：雷娜塔.洛尔
Renate Loll's dislike

721
00:38:08,750 --> 00:38:11,540
对弦理论的额外维度的厌恶
for the extra dimensions of string theory

722
00:38:11,650 --> 00:38:13,440
使其全力以赴
is matched only by her passion

723
00:38:13,550 --> 00:38:16,740
去对付创造出来有待解决的同样的难题 -
to attack the same puzzle it was created to solve --

724
00:38:16,850 --> 00:38:20,410
引力之谜
the mystery of gravity.

725
00:38:20,520 --> 00:38:24,280
爱因斯坦认为引力可以被视为
Einstein realized that gravity could be seen

726
00:38:24,400 --> 00:38:27,350
只不过是物体所弯曲的空间
as simply a bending of space by massive objects.

727
00:38:27,470 --> 00:38:30,060
他的广义相对论
His theory of general relativity

728
00:38:30,170 --> 00:38:33,030
是现代物理学的经典
was a masterpiece of modern physics.

729
00:38:33,140 --> 00:38:36,200
但是它留下了一个重大问题没有解决 -
But it left a serious problem unsolved --

730
00:38:36,310 --> 00:38:41,270
引力是如何在微观层面上影响空间的呢？
how does gravity affect space on the microscopic level?

731
00:38:41,380 --> 00:38:42,470
因此如果你问起
So if you ask questions

732
00:38:42,580 --> 00:38:44,070
必须得说 对于极小极小的
that have to do,say,with the very,very small

733
00:38:44,180 --> 00:38:47,140
牵涉到得与引力打交道的东西 -
and that involves anything that has to do with gravity --

734
00:38:47,250 --> 00:38:50,470
亦即 物体如何与引力互动
so,how do objects interact gravitationally

735
00:38:50,590 --> 00:38:52,040
在很短很短的尺度上 -
on very,very short scales --

736
00:38:52,160 --> 00:38:54,940
于是你就需要有扩展的爱因斯坦理论
then you need an extension of Einstein's theory

737
00:38:55,060 --> 00:38:58,110
因为它并没有涵盖那个范围
because it doesn't cover that range.

738
00:38:58,230 --> 00:39:02,190
弗里曼：雷娜塔接受了那个挑战
Renate has taken on that challenge.

739
00:39:02,300 --> 00:39:05,090
她试图发展新的引力定律
She's trying to develop new laws of gravity

740
00:39:05,200 --> 00:39:08,360
甚至能适用于最小的距离
that apply even at the smallest distances,

741
00:39:08,470 --> 00:39:12,160
她用计算机模拟来测试它们
and she's testing them in computer simulations.

742
00:39:12,280 --> 00:39:15,930
她从空间的微观点的集合入手
She begins with a collection of microscopic points of space

743
00:39:16,050 --> 00:39:20,600
尝试用引力将它们结合在一起
and attempts to stick them together with gravity.

744
00:39:20,720 --> 00:39:23,780
换句话说 她在培养空间
In other words,she is growing space.

745
00:39:23,890 --> 00:39:26,340
上一次这个发生在计算机外面
The last time this happened outside a computer

746
00:39:26,460 --> 00:39:30,180
那是在约137亿年前
was about 13.7 billion years ago.

747
00:39:30,300 --> 00:39:32,280
那是你听说过的事件的一部分 -
It was part of an event you've probably heard of --

748
00:39:32,400 --> 00:39:34,990
大爆炸
the Big Bang.

749
00:39:35,100 --> 00:39:38,060
雷娜塔在小得多的尺度上研究
Renate is working on a much smaller scale,

750
00:39:38,170 --> 00:39:41,430
但她所培养的微观宇宙
but the microscopic Universes she is cultivating

751
00:39:41,540 --> 00:39:44,130
具有某些意想不到的属性
have some very unexpected properties.

752
00:39:44,240 --> 00:39:47,200
设想你有一个空间 或就一块空间
Imagine you're given a space or just a piece of space

753
00:39:47,310 --> 00:39:50,900
你想了解它是什么 尤其是
and you want to learn about what it is,and,in particular,

754
00:39:51,020 --> 00:39:54,010
你可能想了解它的维度
you may want to learn about what its dimension is.

755
00:39:54,120 --> 00:39:58,010
那么有个实验是你其实可以做的
So one experiment that you can actually do

756
00:39:58,120 --> 00:40:00,050
以发现其维度
to find out what the dimension is,

757
00:40:00,160 --> 00:40:04,880
那就是滴一滴墨水在里面 然后看其所发生的情况
is to let an ink drop fall in it and then see what happens,

758
00:40:05,000 --> 00:40:08,860
看看墨水在空间的扩散
see how the ink spreads in the space.

759
00:40:08,970 --> 00:40:13,130
弗里曼：在水里 墨水向三个方向扩散
In water,ink spreads into three dimensions.

760
00:40:13,240 --> 00:40:17,860
在吸墨水纸上 它向两个方向扩散
On a piece of blotting paper,it spreads into two.

761
00:40:17,980 --> 00:40:20,430
然而当雷娜塔在她的计算机模拟宇宙间
But when Renate tested how things spread out

762
00:40:20,550 --> 00:40:23,300
物体是如何扩散时
inside her computer-simulated Universes,

763
00:40:23,410 --> 00:40:26,120
其结果看上去是这种模样
the results looked something like this.

764
00:40:29,220 --> 00:40:32,940
洛尔：现在来看看所发生的情况
Watch what happens now.

765
00:40:33,060 --> 00:40:36,710
它在小尺度上的扩张
It filled out much less ones than we expected

766
00:40:36,830 --> 00:40:37,910
远不及我们的预料
on small scales,

767
00:40:38,030 --> 00:40:39,550
那真正表明了
and that's a true indication

768
00:40:39,660 --> 00:40:42,320
维度其实要小于
that the dimension's actually smaller

769
00:40:42,430 --> 00:40:43,720
我们的预料
than what we expected.

770
00:40:43,830 --> 00:40:45,260
它小于三个
It's smaller than three.

771
00:40:45,370 --> 00:40:46,920
弗里曼：雷娜塔的模拟
Renate's simulations

772
00:40:47,040 --> 00:40:49,230
看上去好像它们有三个维度
looked like they had three dimensions,

773
00:40:49,340 --> 00:40:53,060
但归根结底 它们只有一个
but at root,they only had one.

774
00:40:53,180 --> 00:40:55,360
如果她的引力理论正确的话
If her theories of gravity are right,

775
00:40:55,480 --> 00:41:00,240
那就表明实体空间根本就不是实体
it suggests that solid space is not solid at all.

776
00:41:00,350 --> 00:41:02,840
下至最小的尺度
Down at the smallest scales,

777
00:41:02,950 --> 00:41:07,650
它有可能是一维的线网所构成
it might be built from a mesh of one-dimensional lines.

778
00:41:14,690 --> 00:41:19,020
这就是空间如何构成的基本真理么？
Is this the fundamental truth about how space is formed?

779
00:41:19,130 --> 00:41:23,060
就只有一维是真正存在的么？
Is one dimension all there really is?

780
00:41:23,170 --> 00:41:27,830
这样一来 人们就认为空间的维度
So the order is,one would think of the dimension of a space

781
00:41:27,940 --> 00:41:29,770
是固定的 是上帝赋予的
as fixed,just God-given.

782
00:41:29,880 --> 00:41:31,130
它就在那里
It's just there.

783
00:41:31,250 --> 00:41:34,000
但在极小的尺度上又是怎么回事呢？
But what happens on very,very small scales?

784
00:41:34,120 --> 00:41:37,170
我们发现的故事全然不同
And there's the story we find is totally different.

785
00:41:37,290 --> 00:41:41,780
空间似乎具有越来越小的维度
The space appears to have a smaller and smaller dimension

786
00:41:41,890 --> 00:41:45,150
伴随着你在越来越小的尺度上去探索它
as you explore it on smaller and smaller scales.

787
00:41:45,260 --> 00:41:47,920
弗里曼：其他科学家并不相信
Other scientists are not convinced

788
00:41:48,030 --> 00:41:50,820
雷娜塔的一维宇宙是正确的
Renate's one-dimensional Universe is correct.

789
00:41:50,930 --> 00:41:52,590
他们的赌注都押在了
Their bets are hedged on a Universe

790
00:41:52,700 --> 00:41:55,390
宇宙具有许多额外维度上
with many extra dimensions.

791
00:41:55,510 --> 00:41:58,160
真相依然扑朔迷离
The truth is still elusive.

792
00:41:58,280 --> 00:42:00,430
不过它已不是遥不可及
But it's not out of reach.

793
00:42:00,540 --> 00:42:02,230
兰德尔：这个问题我们确实想要解决
It's a problem we really want to solve.

794
00:42:02,350 --> 00:42:03,900
我们确实认为必须得有个答案 -
We really think there has to be an answer --

795
00:42:04,020 --> 00:42:06,100
确实告诉我们东西必须存在
really tells us that something has to be there,

796
00:42:06,220 --> 00:42:07,440
它能够告诉我们
and it could tell us

797
00:42:07,550 --> 00:42:10,640
存在有某些怪异的基本物质
that there's some really exotic,underlying matter

798
00:42:10,760 --> 00:42:13,510
或物理学 或力量是我们尚未想到过的
or physics or forces that we haven't thought about yet.

799
00:42:13,630 --> 00:42:16,920
最后 就是某种理论
In the end,there is,you know,some theory.

800
00:42:17,030 --> 00:42:19,250
有某种简单优雅的理论出现
There's some simple,elegant theory out there

801
00:42:19,370 --> 00:42:21,720
来阐述整个大自然 我们所看到的一切
that accounts for all of nature,for everything we see,

802
00:42:21,830 --> 00:42:24,860
我们觉得我们能够与其非常密切
and we feel like we could be very,very close to it.

803
00:42:24,970 --> 00:42:28,330
所以一旦你有了骇人的问题
So when you have shocking questions,

804
00:42:28,440 --> 00:42:32,130
有时就会需要骇人的想法和答案
it takes sometimes shocking ideas and answers

805
00:42:32,240 --> 00:42:35,700
努力让你去拥抱它
to try to put your arms around this.

806
00:42:35,810 --> 00:42:40,970
是九个维度呢还是只有一个呢？
Are there nine dimensions or only one?

807
00:42:41,090 --> 00:42:46,610
这个隐匿的空间是弯曲或是卷曲在小小的循环里么？
Is this hidden space warped or curled up in tiny loops?

808
00:42:46,730 --> 00:42:48,450
我们尚不知晓
We don't know yet.

809
00:42:48,560 --> 00:42:51,850
不过我们始终能够确定一件事
But we can be evermore sure of one thing.

810
00:42:51,970 --> 00:42:55,460
我们认为我们所在的三维世界
The three-dimensional world we thought we lived in

811
00:42:55,570 --> 00:42:58,190
是我们唯一能看到的
is only what we see.

812
00:42:58,310 --> 00:43:02,940
现实几乎肯定要陌生得多
Reality is almost certainly a lot stranger.

813
00:43:04,610 --> 00:43:05,250
-- 感谢观赏 --

